# English-only GitHub release notes

Chat with the user may stay Chinese. GitHub Release bodies, updater
`latest.json` notes, and `pnpm release:publish -NotesFile` content must be
English.

## Required

- Write the release title, body, and updater notes in English.
- Translate user-facing change lists before publishing. Do not paste Chinese
  chat summaries into `-NotesFile` or `gh release`.
- Prefer short product bullets: what shipped, who it helps, how to run the ZIP.
- Keep identifiers as-is (`25002001`, `HBSS`, `_m001`, `pnpm version:bump`).

## Forbidden

- Chinese, Japanese, or Korean prose in GitHub Release notes or `latest.json`.
- Mixing an English header with CJK bullets.
- Using `git log` subjects as notes when those subjects contain CJK. Rewrite
  the notes in English first.

## Publisher gate

`pnpm release:publish` rejects notes that contain CJK. Fix the notes file or
commit messages, then publish again.

